-- The diversified starter bank (backlog P3, "the single biggest gameplay
-- quality gap"). The original 550-row starter_seed bank generated all 11 of
-- a state's questions from ONE subject, so any player who saw one question
-- knew every answer for that state for the rest of the season. Its rows are
-- deactivated (kept for history) and replaced by 550 hand-written
-- starter_seed_v2 rows: 11 per state (3 tier-1 two-option MC, 4 tier-2
-- four-option MC, 4 tier-3 free-fill), each state mixing teams, players,
-- venues and events with at least nine distinct answers, alias lists built
-- for answer_matches (nickname alone, last name alone), and sport codes
-- that actually match the SPORTS filter the picker uses (the old bank's
-- "NCAA Football" never matched "CFB"). Still starter content -- the
-- externally validated generation pipeline remains the trivia phase's job.

update public.questions set active = false where validation_status = 'starter_seed';

